### 0. Login as admin
# @name loginAdmin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@gmail.com",
  "password": "abc12345"
}

###

### 0b. Login as customer
# @name loginCustomer
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "farah@gmail.com",
  "password": "abc12345"
}

###

### 1. Create an event with only 1 seat, for boundary testing
# @name tinyEvent
POST http://localhost:8080/api/events
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Last Seat Test",
  "description": "capacity=1 to test the atomic guard",
  "category": "Tech",
  "eventDate": "2026-09-15T18:00:00",
  "venue": "Test Hall",
  "capacity": 1,
  "price": 0
}

###

### 2. Create a PAST event, for the past-date rule
# @name pastEvent
POST http://localhost:8080/api/events
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Already Happened",
  "description": "eventDate in the past",
  "category": "Tech",
  "eventDate": "2020-01-01T18:00:00",
  "venue": "Test Hall",
  "capacity": 10,
  "price": 0
}

###

### 3. Book the 1 available seat -> expect 201, seatsAvailable becomes 0
POST http://localhost:8080/api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "{{tinyEvent.response.body.$.id}}",
  "seatsRequested": 1
}

###

### 4. Book it again -> expect 409 "Not enough seats available"
POST http://localhost:8080/api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "{{tinyEvent.response.body.$.id}}",
  "seatsRequested": 1
}

###

### 5. Confirm via GET that seatsAvailable is exactly 0, not negative
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events/{{tinyEvent.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}

###

### 6. Book a past event -> expect 400 "Cannot book a past event"
POST http://localhost:8080/api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "{{pastEvent.response.body.$.id}}",
  "seatsRequested": 1
}

###

### 7. Book a cancelled event -> expect 400 "Event is cancelled"
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/events/{{pastEvent.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}

###

POST http://localhost:8080/api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "{{pastEvent.response.body.$.id}}",
  "seatsRequested": 1
}

###

### 8. Book a non-existent event -> expect 404
POST http://localhost:8080/api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "000000000000000000000000",
  "seatsRequested": 1
}